.Rhistory
.RData
*.parquet
*.rds

# Bulk data stays out of git. Written as `data/*` rather than `data/` so the
# negation below can take effect: git does not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so `data/` + `!data/x` silently keeps ignoring x.
data/*
# ...but world_records.csv is hand-maintained REFERENCE data, not bulk data.
# It is small, reviewable, and every "% of world record" on the site is wrong
# without it — so it belongs in git.
!data/world_records.csv

# Blog export staging dir — build artefacts, republished on every run
blog/
